--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
About this fork
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is a fork of https://github.com/Philippcmd/SuperVanishV3.

Remotes:
    origin      this fork
    upstream    https://github.com/Philippcmd/SuperVanishV3

The fork exists to split SuperVanish into two halves:

    library/    the visibility engine, with no JavaPlugin, no plugin.yml, no
                static singletons and no assumption that it owns a data folder.
                Persistence is an interface (VanishStateStore) and the audience
                rule is an interface (VanishAudience), so an embedding host
                supplies both.

    src/        the SuperVanish plugin itself, now a thin lifecycle shim that
                builds a VanishService, wires the existing /vanish, /supervanish,
                /vanish-show and /vanish-list commands to it, and registers the
                library's listener.

The upstream plugin behaviour is preserved: same commands, same permissions,
same players.yml (the legacy `vanished` / `super-vanished` lists are still read
so state survives the upgrade).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Downstream use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The SilentAdmin project vendors this repository as a git submodule and compiles
only `library/` into its own Paper module. It does not load SuperVanish as a
Bukkit plugin, does not instantiate dev.philippcmd.supervanish.Main, and does
not register the /vanish command family or the vanish.* permission tree.

The MIT copyright notice above travels with the vendored sources, which is why
the library keeps its original package name.
